selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"ChannelPlacement.html#pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement.ChannelPlacement\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement.ChannelPlacement\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">ChannelPlacement</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">n_channel_positions</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">channel_angular_width</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">occludes</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">bool</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">True</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">helix_angle</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Base class defining how coolant channels are wound around the contour.</p><p>A placement owns the circumferential packing and the winding rate; where a\nsection then sits radially is resolved from the cross section and the wall\nstack rather than from the placement. On its own this class describes\nplain axial channels, and subclasses (surface, internal) refine it.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"InternalPlacement.html#pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement.InternalPlacement\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement.InternalPlacement\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">InternalPlacement</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">n_channel_positions</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">n_channels_per_leaf</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">channel_angular_width</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">occludes</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">bool</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">False</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">helix_angle</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">ChannelPlacement</span></code></p><p>Placement model for in-wall or in-chamber heat-exchanger channels.</p><p>Allows multiple stacked channels per angular leaf and optional\nuser-defined angular-width laws.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"SurfacePlacement.html#pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement.SurfacePlacement\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement.SurfacePlacement\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">SurfacePlacement</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">n_channel_positions</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">helix_angle</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">channel_angular_width</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">ChannelPlacement</span></code></p><p>Placement model for surface-mounted cooling channels.</p><p>Channels are positioned just outside the main wall stack,\noffset by total thickness and corrected for local contour angle.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"ChannelKeepOut.html#pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement.ChannelKeepOut\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement.ChannelKeepOut\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">ChannelKeepOut</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">x_start</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">x_end</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">width</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">count</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">1</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">angle</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">taper</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'keep-out'</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Circumferential sectors of the wall that surface channels must leave clear.</p><p>A keep-out is room reserved in the channel layer for something else, such\nas hardware passing through the wall. It is not a circuit: it carries no\nflow, is not solved, drawn or exported. It acts twice. Every surface\nchannel present in its span shares only the circumference it leaves free,\nso all of them narrow a little and the thermal solve sees that. And the\nnumerical layout pins it as an obstacle, so the channels next to it bend\naside while the rest spread to close up behind them.</p><p>Circuits whose placement states its own <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">channel_angular_width</span></code> keep\nthat width and ignore keep-outs.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#classes\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Classes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#classes\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"#module-pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><h2>Classes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#classes\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 600, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
